WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.819
In this video, we'll turn practice
research into findings with real

2
00:00:11.819 --> 00:00:17.090
quotes, then build the next iteration,
and open a draft pull request.

3
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:20.376
This is a real run, with the waits sped up.

4
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:26.856
Your copy has three practice files:
study results, a design review, and feedback.

5
00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:29.887
They're fictional, written for this workshop.

6
00:00:33.157 --> 00:00:35.420
Six people tried a labeled toolbar.

7
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.881
Here's how they did, what they said,
and what the researcher noticed.

8
00:00:41.876 --> 00:00:45.229
The prompt asks for the
top findings, each with

9
00:00:45.229 --> 00:00:48.724
real quotes and how many
of the six it came from.

10
00:00:48.724 --> 00:00:53.504
Then the next iteration, a draft
pull request, and a findings page.

11
00:00:57.949 --> 00:01:00.589
It reads all three files, and the review

12
00:01:00.589 --> 00:01:03.493
page from earlier, then starts a new branch.

13
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.020
The design review picked
a different direction.

14
00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:14.246
It says so, keeps our favorite,
and applies the strongest findings to it.

15
00:01:15.466 --> 00:01:18.419
It writes a findings page, makes the change,

16
00:01:18.419 --> 00:01:21.574
and checks it in the browser,
next to the chat.

17
00:01:23.444 --> 00:01:27.987
The findings page is in the browser now,
with each quote taken from the files.

18
00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:36.892
Then the fix: five circles in a row,
without picking the tool again.

19
00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:44.013
It opens a draft pull request,
and links the findings from the review page.

20
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:50.089
Each finding has quotes from the files,
and how many of the six it came from.

21
00:01:50.089 --> 00:01:54.638
Repeat drawing was the biggest blocker:
only three of six finished that task.

22
00:01:56.635 --> 00:02:01.156
It also says what it tested, and what
it didn't, like choosing an image file.

23
00:02:05.165 --> 00:02:08.183
The findings page sits next
to your page for everyone,

24
00:02:08.183 --> 00:02:10.363
labeled as fictional practice research.

25
00:02:14.615 --> 00:02:17.830
It ends with what changed,
and what to test next.

26
00:02:22.365 --> 00:02:27.391
The draft pull request explains why,
and what changed. Nothing is merged.

27
00:02:30.865 --> 00:02:34.877
And the next iteration:
Keep tool is now Repeat tool,

28
00:02:34.877 --> 00:02:39.419
with a clear on and off,
and Insert image stays in the dock.

29
00:02:43.327 --> 00:02:45.369
Next, we'll plan an overnight run.
